    "head_branch": "feature/unit-store-native-seek",
    "head_commit_message": "feat(formation): the native seek reads and writes the unit store\n\nSpec 35 step 4b. BodyField.seek replaces plan: GDScript sends only\nwhat its rules say of each fighting squad (its foes, whether it may\nseek, its frame, its chasers) and each unit's speed. The field gathers\nthe rest itself: each unit's place from the store's rank and column\n(SquadFrame.place_in in GDScript's precision), its goal from the\ncolumns, who may seek from the unit's record (preferred band and\nfootprint, now enrolled once). It writes the outcome into the loose\nentry's columns there, as ScrumSeekField's write-back did, and returns\nthe active squads and the batch the walk and the facing still take.\n\nTests: test_body_field.gd checks a synced unit's record on the field\n(red on the old library); the seek parity tests run unchanged through\nthe new path.\n\nWaived-by: Decision 142\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YWpV2AHWr3d2v4fKRki8G7",
